<<<
+ And yet Mr. Barnstaple had the most subile & indefeasible doubt whether indeed Serpentine was speaking, indent. See Noun & VERB ACCENT. independence, -cy. The -cy form retains only some special senses— Congregationalism, an independent State, & an independent income— ; & in these, though still preferred to -ce, is now usually displaced by Congregationalism, sovereign or independent State, & competency.
===
+ *And yet Mr. Barnstaple had the most subtle & indefeasible doubt whether indeed Serpentine was speaking.*

**indent.** See ^^NOUN^^ & ^^VERB ACCENT^^.

**independence, -cy.** The *-cy* form retains only some special senses—Congregationalism, an independent State, & an independent income—; & in these, though still preferred to *-ce*, is now usually displaced by *Congregationalism, sovereign or independent State, & competency.*
>>>

